---
import SocialList from "@/components/SocialList.astro";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description: "I'm a starter theme for Astro.build",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-6">About</h1>

	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none space-y-6">
		<p>
			Wubba Lubba dub-dub - I'm Kushagra, `kush1jpeg` in the parts of the internet that matter.
			Say my name three times and I'll appear in front of you explaining why Arch is the only right choice
			u'll ever make and why you should be using Neovim (I'm still learning both, but the conviction is unwavering).

		</p>


		<p>
			I'm a third-year CS student who fell down the rabbit hole of systems programming and everything that lives close to the metal makes my platonic mind erupt:
			kernels, compilers(<em>will_build.future_inPain</em>), linux-ricing, systems,
			<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4K8IEzXnMYk" target="_blank">but still, am not him</a>.
      
      <p/>

		<p>
      My current, is backend engineering and distributed systems. I find this stuff genuinely
			beautiful in a way I can't fully explain to people who haven't felt it, ofcourse not at par
			with the low level stuff: but definitely serves as a more socially acceptable replacement to it /ifykyk

      <p/>
		<p>
			To maintain some illusion of employability (and a little sanity for the people around me) i have to get my hands dirty inside dumbo-abstracted languages
			for web dev and insert buzzword framework in the resume.
			Yes, I know AI is coming for my job. I just hope it takes me out quickly.



	<img
	src="/camus1.jpg"
	alt="Camus"
	class="float-right ml-6 mb-4 w-56 border-2 border-gray-400 rounded-xl"
  />

			<br />
			<br />

			Philosophically speaking-
			<span class="text-sm font-light italic text-emerald-300 rounded">
				i really hate that ubermensch dream
			</span>,
			of a certain guy with the big mustache :>
			trying to follow Camus' absurd way of living — "Life is meaningless"
		</p>
		<p>
			Not only i follow Camus' ideology, like him - I drink more coffee than is medically advisable with a death-stick in one hand.
      The aim is to become a hybrid athelete or as the saying goes-

			<div class="text-sm font-light italic text-purple-300 rounded">
        "OUTrun the runners, <br>
        OUTlift the lifters, <br>
        OUTdrink the drinkers"
      </div>
		</p>

			If you made it this far, congratulations -
			You now know more about me than my extended family.
			For everything else -
		</p>

    <div class="my-6 flex justify-center">
	<SocialList />
	</div>
</PageLayout>
